% ============================================================================
% homophones.query.adj — a worked recall over the word-homophones library.
% ============================================================================
% The shape a learner (or an LLM) produces to ANSWER "what sounds the same
% as there?": it states no fact of its own — it only `import`s the grounded
% table and asks binding queries. The engine resolves each `?` against the
% `homophone` rows and returns EVERY sound-alike word + the table's own
% source/locator/trust (as of this cycle's extension, a bound word can
% recall MULTIPLE sound-alikes — `there` now recalls their ; theyre, and
% `to` now recalls too ; two). A word the table does not carry abstains
% honestly — the engine never invents a homophone.
%
% Run (from this directory so the relative import resolves):
%     ../../../../packages/rust/target/debug/adj-lang-cli homophones.query.adj
% ============================================================================

import "homophones.adj"

? homophone(there, $Word)      % expect their ; theyre
? homophone(to, $Word)         % expect too ; two (added this cycle)
? homophone($Word, too)        % expect to
? homophone(here, $Word)       % expect abstain — no homophone is shipped for here
